sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch12-31> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "If questions about the long-run evolution of a multiway system (an idealized axiom system) are undecidable, then the system cannot be both complete and consistent, because completeness plus consistency would give a procedure that always terminates to decide whether a string is reached.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An irreducible multiway system cannot be both complete and consistent";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 12, “The Principle of Computational Equivalence”; section “Implications for Mathematics and Its Foundations” (from p. 772), p. 783. Scope: multiway systems interpreted as axiom systems with a negation operation"
}
